BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌌 Leonids meteor shower peak (est.)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:ff798a2c70e2fb5b09d4@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:Fastest meteors of the year at 71 km/s. Famous for historic st
 orms\; usually a modest show nowadays. Up to ~15/hr under perfect skies (r
 ealistically a fraction of that). 🌓 Moon 56% lit: decent\, observe whil
 e it's below the horizon.\n\nStatus: 🟡 Estimated (pattern-based or prov
 isional\; check before booking)\nPeak night shown\; the night either side 
 is usually worthwhile too.\nOfficial info: https://www.imo.net/resources/c
 alendar/
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.imo.net/resources/calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌌 Full Beaver Moon (Supermoon)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:69b78dc8ac3f042cdc3c@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:Full Beaver Moon (Supermoon): the time to set traps before the
  swamps froze. Peak at 14:53 UK time\; catch it rising at dusk on the even
 ing closest to the peak for the classic giant-on-the-horizon photo. Only 3
 60\,765 km away\, up to ~14% bigger and ~30% brighter than a micromoon.\n
 \nStatus: ✅ Confirmed\nExact full moon: Tue 24 Nov 2026 14:53 GMT. Earth
 –Moon distance 360\,765 km.
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
