DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:4dfe902017b945f8b9e5@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:Full Cold Moon (Supermoon): the long-nights moon\, riding high
 est in the sky of the whole year. Peak at 01:28 UK time\; catch it rising 
 at dusk on the evening closest to the peak for the classic giant-on-the-ho
 rizon photo. Only 356\,738 km away\, up to ~14% bigger and ~30% brighter t
 han a micromoon.\n\nStatus: ✅ Confirmed\nExact full moon: Thu 24 Dec 202
 6 01:28 GMT. Earth–Moon distance 356\,738 km.
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌌 Quadrantids meteor shower peak (est.)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:4b2c0b1728c598f3dad3@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:Short\, sharp peak of only a few hours\, so it's a gamble\, bu
 t one of the year's strongest. Radiant high in the north-east after midnig
 ht. Up to ~110/hr under perfect skies (realistically a fraction of that). 
 🌑 Moon only 12% lit: excellent\, dark skies.\n\nStatus: 🟡 Estimated 
 (pattern-based or provisional\; check before booking)\nPeak night shown\; 
 the night either side is usually worthwhile too.\nOfficial info: https://w
 ww.imo.net/resources/calendar/
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.imo.net/resources/calendar/
