BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌌 Penumbral lunar eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270221
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:3845bd435db03e8998a6@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:The Moon slips into Earth's faint outer shadow. It's a subtle 
 dusky shading on one side rather than a red 'blood moon'\, but it's a nice
  excuse to look up\, and it's the warm-up for the eclipse season ahead.\n
 \nStatus: ✅ Confirmed\nPenumbral eclipses are subtle\; best seen near ma
 ximum. Check timeanddate for exact local times.\nOfficial info: https://ww
 w.timeanddate.com/eclipse/in/uk
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/in/uk
END:VEVENT
