BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌌 Aurora watch: equinox boost window (est.)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270311
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
UID:e2521edee9c2499c52b5@global-events-calendar
CATEGORIES:Sky & Nature (UK)
DESCRIPTION:Geomagnetic storms are statistically more likely in the weeks 
 around the equinoxes\, because of how Earth's field lines up with the sola
 r wind. Get AuroraWatch UK alerts on your phone and take every clear night
  seriously.\n\nStatus: 🟡 Estimated (pattern-based or provisional\; chec
 k before booking)\nStatistical window (late Feb–early April)\, not a for
 ecast.\nOfficial info: https://aurorawatch.lancs.ac.uk
GEO:58.5;-3.5
LOCATION:Northern Scotland best\; often visible further south during storm
 s
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://aurorawatch.lancs.ac.uk
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE="Northern
  Scotland best; often visible further south during storms":geo:58.5,-3.5
END:VEVENT
