 h's dark umbra\, turning a coppery red with just a bright sliver left. The
  best lunar eclipse from the UK in this window. Set an alarm\; it's worth 
 it.\n\nStatus: ✅ Confirmed\nVisible roughly 02:30–05:30 GMT\; maximum 
 ~04:03 GMT.\nLocal start: Wed 12 Jan 04:03 (GMT). Your calendar shows it i
 n your own time zone.\nOfficial info: https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/
 in/uk
LOCATION:Visible across the UK
URL:https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/in/uk
END:VEVENT
